IMPORT prelude

-- Jewish Synagogue Ordinance 1878 (Singapore) -- who may sell the Synagogue Street land (s 2), what the proceeds may be spent on
-- (s 3), when a buyer is safe (s 4), the trust of the new synagogue land and when it reverts to the Government (s 5), what the
-- conveyance of the new land must say (s 6), who may appoint new trustees and when only the High Court can (s 7), and what vests
-- in new trustees without a transfer (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/JSO1878.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The amendment
-- annotations in the body are "[7/97]" under s 5(2), "[42/2005; 40/2019]" under s 7(2), and "[Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]"
-- under s 7(2). The Ordinance is dated 29 March 1878.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0236 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance has eight sections, so the whole of it is in scope except the short
-- title. For a person outside the trust it matters in two places: buying from the trustees (ss 2, 4), and the Government's
-- reversion if the synagogue land stops being used for Jewish worship (s 5(2)). For a member of the Jewish community it says who
-- may apply to the High Court when the trustees fall below three (s 7(2)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the recitals (the 1841 lease and its resumption proviso, the 1876 Aleppo deed) except as
-- background; whether the s 2 sale has already happened (the Ordinance does not say; the arrangement of sections reads as if it
-- has, but that is an inference); what "think proper" in s 2 or "suitable" in ss 5(1) and 7(2) requires; the procedure on an
-- originating application.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Jewish Synagogue Ordinance 1878 -- the trust`

DECLARE Property IS ONE OF
    `the Synagogue Street land`
    `the buildings on the Synagogue Street land`
    `the new synagogue land`
    `the new synagogue building`
    `fixtures of the synagogue`
    `furniture of the synagogue`
    `other movable property of the synagogue for Divine worship`
    `a trustee's own house`

§§ `2 -- who may sell the Synagogue Street land`

-- s 2: "The said Joshua Raphael Joshua, Ezra Abraham Solomon, Salleh Menasseh, Menasseh Meyer, Reuben Meyer, Sassoon Aaron Gubbay,
-- and David Aaron Gubbay as trustees of the Jewish Synagogue of Singapore, or the survivors of them, or any 2 or more of such
-- surviving trustees, who are for the time being resident within the Colony may sell and dispose of the said piece or parcel of
-- land comprised in and demised by the hereinbefore recited indenture of lease ... dated 1 September 1841, and also all erections
-- and buildings which have been erected, and are now standing on the said premises", with power to "execute assurances, give
-- effectual receipts for the purchase money, and do all other acts and things for completing such sale".
--
-- The power is given to the seven NAMED trustees and their survivors. s 2 does not extend it to trustees appointed later under
-- s 7 (encoded as written; whether s 8's vesting carries the power with the property is not said). "who are for the time being
-- resident within the Colony" is read as qualifying every seller (an inference from the punctuation). That all the survivors
-- together may sell even if only one survives is an inference from "or the survivors of them"; the text does not say so.
DECLARE Sellers HAS
    `number of sellers` IS A NUMBER
    `every seller is one of the seven named trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `every seller is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sellers are all the surviving named trustees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sellers` IS A Sellers
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sellers hold the power of sale` IF
        `the sellers`'s `every seller is one of the seven named trustees`
    AND `the sellers`'s `every seller is resident in Singapore`
    AND (    `the sellers`'s `the sellers are all the surviving named trustees`
         OR  `the sellers`'s `number of sellers` >= 2)

GIVEN `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is within the power of sale` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `the Synagogue Street land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the buildings on the Synagogue Street land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the sellers` IS A Sellers, `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale is authorised by s 2` IF
    `the sellers hold the power of sale` `the sellers` AND `the property is within the power of sale` `the property`

§§ `3 -- what the proceeds may be spent on`

-- s 3(1): "The moneys to arise from such sale, after deducting the cost and expenses attending the sale or otherwise incurred in
-- relation thereto, shall be paid to the trustees ... for the purpose of acquiring land, and erecting and building on such land
-- ... a new synagogue or place of worship for the use of the members of the Jewish community in Singapore."
-- s 3(2): "Such moneys shall be applied by such trustees to the purchase of such land and the building of such synagogue, and to
-- no other purpose."
-- s 3(3): the land and building "shall be held subject to the trust set out in this Ordinance".
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `paying the costs and expenses of the sale`
    `buying land for the new synagogue`
    `building the new synagogue`
    `repairing the old synagogue`
    `relief of poor members of the community`
    `investing for income`
    `paying the rabbi`

GIVEN `the gross price` IS A NUMBER, `the costs of the sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the net proceeds payable to the trustees` IS
    `the gross price` - `the costs of the sale`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale money may go to` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `paying the costs and expenses of the sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying land for the new synagogue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `building the new synagogue` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- the buyer's discharge`

-- s 4: "The receipts for the purchase money given by the persons exercising the power of sale hereby conferred shall be sufficient
-- discharges to the purchasers who shall not be bound to see to the application of such purchase money."
--
-- The buyer is safe if the receipt comes from persons who hold the s 2 power. What the trustees then do with the money is not the
-- buyer's concern, even if they breach s 3(2).
GIVEN `the givers of the receipt` IS A Sellers, `the trustees misapplied the money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer is discharged` IF
    `the sellers hold the power of sale` `the givers of the receipt`

§§ `5 and 6 -- the new land: the trust, the reversion and the conveyance`

-- s 5(1): the land purchased "shall be held by the said trustees and their successors in office as trustees for the use of the
-- Jewish community of Singapore for the purpose of erecting and maintaining thereon a suitable synagogue or place of Divine worship
-- according to the Jewish form."
-- s 5(2) (side note "When to be forfeited"): "So soon as the said piece of land ceases to be used for such purpose it shall ipso
-- facto revert to the Government." [7/97]
-- s 6: the conveyance to the trustees of any lands paid for out of the proceeds "shall express that the said lands are conveyed to,
-- and are to be held by them subject to the trust and condition set out in this Ordinance."
--
-- "the said piece of land" in s 5(2) is the phrase the recitals and s 2 use for the Synagogue Street land; it sits in s 5, about the
-- new land. It is encoded as applying to the new land (an inference from its place in s 5 and the side note). The reversion is
-- "ipso facto": no notice, order or re-entry is required on the words. Building a synagogue counts as use "for such purpose"
-- ("erecting and maintaining").
DECLARE LandUse IS ONE OF
    `a synagogue used for Jewish worship`
    `a synagogue being erected`
    `a place of worship of another faith`
    `a community hall`
    `a school`
    `let out commercially`
    `left unused`

GIVEN `the current use` IS A LandUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is used for the trust purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the current use`
    WHEN `a synagogue used for Jewish worship` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a synagogue being erected` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the current use` IS A LandUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land reverts to the Government` IF
    NOT `the land is used for the trust purpose` `the current use`

GIVEN `paid for out of the sale proceeds` IS A BOOLEAN, `the conveyance expresses the trust and condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance complies with s 6` IF
    (NOT `paid for out of the sale proceeds`) OR `the conveyance expresses the trust and condition`

§§ `7 -- new trustees`

-- s 7(1): the trustees "may be styled the 'Trustees of the Jewish Synagogue at Singapore', and they or the remaining trustees,
-- being not less than 3, may at any time appoint new trustees to take the place of such trustees as have died, or left the Colony,
-- or declined further to act."
-- s 7(2): "In the event of the number of trustees at any time falling below 3, the General Division of the High Court, on an
-- originating application made by the remaining trustees or by any of the members of the Jewish community, may appoint suitable
-- persons being members of the Jewish community residing in Singapore to be trustees under this Ordinance."
--
-- With 3 or more left, the trustees appoint; with fewer than 3, only the Court can. s 7(1) names three vacancies; removal of a
-- trustee is not among them, and the Ordinance gives no power to remove. s 7(1) sets no qualification for a trustee-appointed
-- trustee; s 7(2) does for a Court-appointed one.
DECLARE Vacancy IS ONE OF
    `a trustee died`
    `a trustee left Singapore`
    `a trustee declined to act further`
    `the other trustees want a trustee removed`

DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `the remaining trustees`
    `a member of the Jewish community`
    `a neighbour who is not a member of the community`
    `the Government`

GIVEN `trustees remaining` IS A NUMBER, `the vacancy` IS A Vacancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trustees may fill the vacancy` IF
        `trustees remaining` >= 3
    AND CONSIDER `the vacancy`
        WHEN `a trustee died` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a trustee left Singapore` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a trustee declined to act further` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `trustees remaining` IS A NUMBER, `the applicant` IS A Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court may appoint on the application` IF
        `trustees remaining` < 3
    AND CONSIDER `the applicant`
        WHEN `the remaining trustees` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a member of the Jewish community` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `is a member of the Jewish community` IS A BOOLEAN, `resides in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Court may appoint the candidate` IF
    `is a member of the Jewish community` AND `resides in Singapore`

§§ `8 -- vesting without transfer`

-- s 8: "The property of the said trust, including the land, building, fixtures, furniture and other movable property belonging to
-- the synagogue for the purpose of Divine worship shall be held to vest in the Trustees of the Jewish Synagogue at Singapore for the
-- time being without transfer or assignment from trustees to trustees."
--
-- The rule returns FALSE for the Synagogue Street land and its buildings on the footing that, once sold under s 2, they are no
-- longer trust property (an inference: the text does not say whether they were ever sold). No case asserts either way.
GIVEN `the property` IS A Property
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `vests in new trustees without transfer` IF
    CONSIDER `the property`
    WHEN `the new synagogue land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the new synagogue building` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `fixtures of the synagogue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `furniture of the synagogue` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `other movable property of the synagogue for Divine worship` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
